e risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Service Properties Trust is a small-cap real estate business with a $675M market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $107M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 10.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 467% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 71/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 33% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Large open-market insider purchases (net $50.3M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Service Properties Trust (SVC) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/what-service-properties-trust-svc-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793996203.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Service Properties Trust (NASDAQ:SVC) Issues Quarterly Earnings Results, Misses Estimates By $0.39 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/service-properties-trust-nasdaqsvc-issues-quarterly-earnings-results-misses-estimates-by-0-39-eps.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793945780.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.906,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","legal"]},{"title":"Service Properties (SVC) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/properties-svc-q3-2026-earnings-214821000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793916024.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Service Properties Trust (NASDAQ:SVC) Hits New 52-Week Low \u2013 Should You Sell?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"htt