wth of 25.7% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (12.4% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and institutions hold 86%.","Insiders have only bought over the past year (5 purchases, net $50.3M bought).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.1% (0.1% in buybacks and 3.8% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 4.7% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It pays out 467% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["CEO pay is $2K."]},"profile":{"v":"INSUFFICIENT DATA","conv":null,"head":"Not enough data to value it: missing price or fair value.","pros":[],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":null,"vc":null,"med":{"pe":23.5593,"ev_ebitda":16.316,"pfcf":17.832,"pb":1.3568,"roic":0.0411,"gross_margin":0.5765,"fcf_margin":0.1733,"div_yield":0.0479}},"ticker":"SVC","date":"2026-11-06"}